ds#Slash command execution#Completion text reconciliation","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":43},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/dashboardEventAdapter.ts#mergeStreamedWithFinal","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Completion text reconciliation","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":43},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/HistoryRow.tsx#ReasoningRow","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Reasoning & tool activity rows","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":49},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/HistoryRow.tsx#ToolActivityGroup","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Reasoning & tool activity rows","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":49},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/HistoryRow.tsx#toolActivityGroupTitle","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Reasoning & tool activity rows","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":49},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/sessionHistory.ts#dbItemsToChatMessages","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Bubble hover timestamp","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":55},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/sessionHistory.ts#reconcileAfterDbRefresh","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Bubble hover timestamp","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":55},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/MessageRow.tsx#formatBubbleTime","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Bubble hover timestamp","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":55},{"target":"src/shared/chat-approval.ts#normalizeApprovalRequest","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Structured command approvals","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":67},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/ApprovalCard.tsx#ApprovalCard","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Structured command approvals","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":67},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useDashboardChatTransport.ts#useDashboardChatTransport","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Structured command approvals","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":67},{"target":"src/main/hermes.ts#registerPendingApproval","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Structured command approvals","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":69},{"target":"src/main/ipc/register.ts#registerIpcHandlers","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Structured command approvals","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":69},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useChatActions.ts#parseBackgroundCommand","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Side questions (/btw)","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":89},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/Chat.tsx","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Side questions (/btw)","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":89},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useDashboardChatTransport.ts#useDashboardChatTransport","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Side questions (/btw)","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":89},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/handleSlashCommand.ts#handleSlashCommand","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Central command router","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":93},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/commandCatalog.ts#createSlashCatalog","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Central command router","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":97},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/desktopCommands.ts#DESKTOP_SLASH_COMMANDS","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Central command router#Desktop commands","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":101},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useChatActions.ts#useChatActions","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Central command router#Desktop commands","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":103},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Layout/Layout.tsx","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Central command router#Desktop commands","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":105},{"target":"sidebar-navigation#Settings modal","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Central command router#Desktop commands","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":105},{"target":"src/renderer/src/components/settings/SettingsModal.tsx#resolveSection","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Central command router#Desktop commands","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":105},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/executeAgentCommand.ts#executeAgentCommand","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Central command router#Agent commands","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":111},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/prepareModelSubmission.ts#prepareModelSubmission","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Central command router#Model commands","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":115},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/SlashCommandIcon.tsx#SlashCommandIcon","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Central command router#Command icons","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":119},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/SlashCommandIcon.tsx#registerCustomSlashSvg","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Central command router#Command icons","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":121},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/ChatInput.tsx#ChatInput","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Central command router#Command icons","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":123},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/virtualSlashCommands.ts#createSlashCommandVirtualLayout","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Central command router#Command icons","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":127},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/dashboardEventAdapter.ts#appendClarifyRequest","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Dashboard clarification cards","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":133},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/Chat.tsx#Chat","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Dashboard clarification cards","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":133},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/ClarifyCard.tsx","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Dashboard clarification cards","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":133},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useDashboardChatTransport.ts#useDashboardChatTransport","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Dashboard clarification cards","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":133},{"target":"dashboard-clarify","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-commands#Slash command execution#Dashboard clarification cards","file":"lat.md/chat-commands","line":133}],"paragraphs":[{"markdown":"Typed slash commands (`/compact`, `/compress`, `/reset`, `/web`, …) are run through the gateway's command pipeline, not submitted to the model as plain prompt text. This is what makes them _do_ something instead of being echoed back as prose.","startLine":3,"endLine":3,"text":"Typed slash commands (/compact, /compress, /reset, /web, …) are run through the gateway's command pipeline, not submitted to the model as plain prompt text. This is what makes them do something instead of being echoed back as prose."},{"markdown":"The desktop talks to the hermes-agent gateway over JSON-RPC. A normal message goes via `prompt.submit`, which the gateway treats as a user turn — so a literal `/compact` reaches the model and comes back as text. Real commands must instead go through `slash.exec` (registry-backed worker) with a `command.dispatch` fallback for commands that resolve to an alias, plugin, skill, or an agent prompt.","startLine":5,"endLine":5,"text":"The desktop talks to the hermes-agent gateway over JSON-RPC. A normal message goes via prompt.submit, which the gateway treats as a user turn — so a literal /compact reaches the model and comes back as text. Real commands must instead go through slash.exec (registry-backed worker) with a command.dispatch fallback for commands that resolve to an alias, plugin, skill, or an agent prompt."},{"markdown":"The pure routing logic lives in [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slashExec.ts#executeSlash]]: try `slash.exec`, accept either rendered output or a structured dispatch result, and on rejection fall back to `command.dispatch`, returning `done`, `send`, or `error`.","startLine":9,"endLine":9,"text":"The pure routing logic lives in src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slashExec.ts#executeSlash: try slash.exec, accept either rendered output or a structured dispatch result, and on rejection fall back to command.dispatch, returning done, send, or error."},{"markdown":"It mirrors hermes-agent's reference client (`web/src/lib/slashExec.ts`) so every front-end implements the same contract. Pending-input commands such as `/learn` can return `{type: \"send\"}` directly from `slash.exec`; that prompt still passes through the central model-submission path.","startLine":11,"endLine":11,"text":"It mirrors hermes-agent's reference client (web/src/lib/slashExec.ts) so every front-end implements the same contract. Pending-input commands such as /learn can return {type: \"send\"} directly from slash.exec; that prompt still passes through the central model-submission path."},{"markdown":"Every typed slash command is resolved through the merged catalog before execution. Ownership is explicit (`target: \"desktop\" | \"agent\" | \"model\"`); display categories such as `info` do not determine routing.","startLine":15,"endLine":15,"text":"Every typed slash command is resolved through the merged catalog before execution. Ownership is explicit (target: \"desktop\" | \"agent\" | \"model\"); display categories such as info do not determine routing."},{"markdown":"Desktop-only commands delegate to local renderer handlers, Agent commands use the gateway command pipeline, and model commands build a prompt through the shared model-submission formatter. The legacy transport reports Agent commands as unavailable instead of sending raw `/…` text to the model.","startLine":17,"endLine":17,"text":"Desktop-only commands delegate to local renderer handlers, Agent commands use the gateway command pipeline, and model commands build a prompt through the shared model-submission formatter. The legacy transport reports Agent commands as unavailable instead of sending raw /… text to the model."},{"markdown":"Slash commands run on the gateway's **persistent slash-worker subprocess**, concurrent with any in-flight turn — so they respond instantly and must NOT sit in the busy queue behind a running turn (only plain prompts queue).","startLine":21,"endLine":21,"text":"Slash commands run on the gateway's persistent slash-worker subprocess, concurrent with any in-flight turn — so they respond instantly and must NOT sit in the busy queue behind a running turn (only plain prompts queue)."},{"markdown":"`handleSubmitOrQueue` in [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/Chat.tsx]] dispatches every `/…` input immediately to the central router. Desktop and slash-worker commands can complete concurrently; model commands and Agent `send`/skill directives are formatted once and queued when the main model turn is busy.","startLine":23,"endLine":23,"text":"handleSubmitOrQueue in src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/Chat.tsx dispatches every /… input immediately to the central router. Desktop and slash-worker commands can complete concurrently; model commands and Agent send/skill directives are formatted once and queued when the main model turn is busy."},{"markdown":"Because no global loading state is set, the slash branch shows its own feedback: it inserts an in-place `⏳ Running …` agent bubble, buffers the pipeline output, and replaces that bubble with the result (or `error: …`) when the command resolves — otherwise a slow or unreachable gateway would leave the user staring at nothing. Handled UI actions without output silently remove the pending bubble without leaving conversation artifacts.","startLine":25,"endLine":25,"text":"Because no global loading state is set, the slash branch shows its own feedback: it inserts an in-place ⏳ Running … agent bubble, buffers the pipeline output, and replaces that bubble with the result (or error: …) when the command resolves — otherwise a slow or unreachable gateway would leave the user staring at nothing. Handled UI actions without output silently remove the pending bubble without leaving conversation artifacts."},{"markdown":"Every dashboard turn first connects a JSON-RPC WebSocket to the gateway; that handshake must be time-bounded or a stalled socket wedges the whole transport with no error and no fallback (issue #718).","startLine":29,"endLine":29,"text":"Every dashboard turn first connects a JSON-RPC WebSocket to the gateway; that handshake must be time-bounded or a stalled socket wedges the whole transport with no error and no fallback (issue #718)."},{"markdown":"[[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/dashboardGatewayClient.ts#DashboardGatewayClient#connect]] resolves on `open`, rejects on `error` or an early `close`, **and** rejects on a connect-timeout (default 10s). A WebSocket stuck in `CONNECTING` — TCP accepted but the upgrade never completing, e.g. when a busy renderer starves the handshake — fires none of those events on its own, so without the timer the connect promise never settles. When it never settles, `ensureClient` in [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useDashboardChatTransport.ts#useDashboardChatTransport]] never resolves, its cached `connectingRef` promise poisons every later send, `setIsLoading(false)` never runs, and the user sees a permanent loading spinner. The timeout makes the promise reject so auto mode falls back to the legacy HTTP transport (and explicit-dashboard mode surfaces a real error) instead of hanging. Per-request calls are separately bounded by their own 30s timeout.","startLine":31,"endLine":31,"text":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/dashboardGatewayClient.ts#DashboardGatewayClient#connect resolves on open, rejects on error or an early close, and rejects on a connect-timeout (default 10s). A WebSocket stuck in CONNECTING — TCP accepted but the upgrade never completing, e.g. when a busy renderer starves the handshake — fires none of those events on its own, so without the timer the connect promise never settles. When it never settles, ensureClient in src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useDashboardChatTransport.ts#useDashboardChatTransport never resolves, its cached connectingRef promise poisons every later send, setIsLoading(false) never runs, and the user sees a permanent loading spinner. The timeout makes the promise reject so auto mode falls back to the legacy HTTP transport (and explicit-dashboard mode surfaces a real error) instead of hanging. Per-request calls are separately bounded by their own 30s timeout."},{"markdown":"All transcript writers share one synchronous source of truth so streamed deltas cannot be lost between React commits.","startLine":35,"endLine":35,"text":"All transcript writers share one synchronous source of truth so streamed deltas cannot be lost between React commits."},{"markdown":"[[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useTranscriptState.ts#useTranscriptState]] owns both the rendered state and its write-through ref. Dashboard deltas update that ref immediately and may defer the React commit to the next animation frame; user messages, clear, clarification, background replies, and failure marking resolve against the same newest array.","startLine":37,"endLine":37,"text":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useTranscriptState.ts#useTranscriptState owns both the rendered state and its write-through ref. Dashboard deltas update that ref immediately and may defer the React commit to the next animation frame; user messages, clear, clarification, background replies, and failure marking resolve against the same newest array."},{"markdown":"On `message.complete` the desktop reconciles the text streamed via `message.delta` with the turn's `final_response`, because a last-turn-only final would otherwise clobber text streamed before a tool call (#746).","startLine":41,"endLine":41,"text":"On message.complete the desktop reconciles the text streamed via message.delta with the turn's final_response, because a last-turn-only final would otherwise clobber text streamed before a tool call (#746)."},{"markdown":"[[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/dashboardEventAdapter.ts#completeAssistantWithFinalText]] rewrites the last assistant bubble through [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/dashboardEventAdapter.ts#mergeStreamedWithFinal]], which compares whitespace-insensitively and: uses the final text when it already contains the streamed text; keeps the streamed text when it contains the final (preserving pre-tool-call content); stitches a re-streamed boundary by dropping the duplicated word-aligned seam (rejecting coincidental mid-word overlaps); replaces a garbled re-stream with the final text when the two converge on a substantial common suffix (a corrupted-prefix delta — e.g. a mangled CJK stream — that ends the same sentence as the clean final, rather than the disjoint pre-tool-call + answer pair); and otherwise concatenates the two with a blank-line separator so segments never run together. On the remote/SSH path deltas are not rendered (`renderAssistantDeltas: false`), so the bubble starts empty and the final text is used verbatim.","startLine":43,"endLine":43,"text":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/dashboardEventAdapter.ts#completeAssistantWithFinalText rewrites the last assistant bubble through src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/dashboardEventAdapter.ts#mergeStreamedWithFinal, which compares whitespace-insensitively and: uses the final text when it already contains the streamed text; keeps the streamed text when it contains the final (preserving pre-tool-call content); stitches a re-streamed boundary by dropping the duplicated word-aligned seam (rejecting coincidental mid-word overlaps); replaces a garbled re-stream with the final text when the two converge on a substantial common suffix (a corrupted-prefix delta — e.g. a mangled CJK stream — that ends the same sentence as the clean final, rather than the disjoint pre-tool-call + answer pair); and otherwise concatenates the two with a blank-line separator so segments never run together. On the remote/SSH path deltas are not rendered (renderAssistantDeltas: false), so the bubble starts empty and the final text is used verbatim."},{"markdown":"Streamed reasoning and tool calls are folded into compact, collapsible transcript rows rather than stacked bubbles, so a turn with heavy thinking or many tool calls stays scannable.","startLine":47,"endLine":47,"text":"Streamed reasoning and tool calls are folded into compact, collapsible transcript rows rather than stacked bubbles, so a turn with heavy thinking or many tool calls stays scannable."},{"markdown":"[[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/HistoryRow.tsx#ReasoningRow]] renders the `Thought` / `Thinking…` row and [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/HistoryRow.tsx#ToolActivityGroup]] folds a contiguous run of tool calls/results into one row titled by [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/HistoryRow.tsx#toolActivityGroupTitle]]. Each row is collapsed by default and borderless (Codex-style): dim at rest, it brightens and reveals an expand chevron beside the title on hover/focus, and clicking toggles the body open. While the turn is still streaming the leading icon is a `Grid` loader (purple for reasoning, blue for tools); once finished it shows the brain/tool glyph.","startLine":49,"endLine":49,"text":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/HistoryRow.tsx#ReasoningRow renders the Thought / Thinking… row and src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/HistoryRow.tsx#ToolActivityGroup folds a contiguous run of tool calls/results into one row titled by src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/HistoryRow.tsx#toolActivityGroupTitle. Each row is collapsed by default and borderless (Codex-style): dim at rest, it brightens and reveals an expand chevron beside the title on hover/focus, and clicking toggles the body open. While the turn is still streaming the leading icon is a Grid loader (purple for reasoning, blue for tools); once finished it shows the brain/tool glyph."},{"markdown":"Each user/assistant bubble reveals a relative \"time ago\" label on row hover, so the transcript stays uncluttered at rest but is still scrutable when a user wants to know _when_ something was said.","startLine":53,"endLine":53,"text":"Each user/assistant bubble reveals a relative \"time ago\" label on row hover, so the transcript stays uncluttered at rest but is still scrutable when a user wants to know when something was said."},{"markdown":"The canonical time comes from state.db: [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/sessionHistory.ts#dbItemsToChatMessages]] copies each row's `timestamp` onto the `ChatBubbleMessage`, and [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/sessionHistory.ts#reconcileAfterDbRefresh|the end-of-stream reconcile]] adopts it onto the matching streamed bubble (via `mergeDbMetadataIntoStreamed`) so a live turn picks up its real time after refresh without remounting. state.db stores times in **seconds**, so `toEpochMs` in MessageRow scales any sub-`1e12` value up to milliseconds before use (otherwise it renders as ~Jan 1970). [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/MessageRow.tsx#formatBubbleTime]] builds the label with date-fns `formatDistanceToNowStrict` (e.g. \"5 minutes ago\", \"just now\" under 10s), with `formatBubbleTimeAbsolute` supplying the exact date/time as the `<time>` element's `title`/`dateTime`. The `.chat-message:hover .chat-bubble-time` CSS fades it in below the bubble, anchored to `.chat-message` because `.chat-bubble`'s own `overflow` would clip it.","startLine":55,"endLine":55,"text":"The canonical time comes from state.db: src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/sessionHistory.ts#dbItemsToChatMessages copies each row's timestamp onto the ChatBubbleMessage, and the end-of-stream reconcile adopts it onto the matching streamed bubble (via mergeDbMetadataIntoStreamed) so a live turn picks up its real time after refresh without remounting. state.db stores times in seconds, so toEpochMs in MessageRow scales any sub-1e12 value up to milliseconds before use (otherwise it renders as ~Jan 1970). src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/MessageRow.tsx#formatBubbleTime builds the label with date-fns formatDistanceToNowStrict (e.g. \"5 minutes ago\", \"just now\" under 10s), with formatBubbleTimeAbsolute supplying the exact date/time as the <time> element's title/dateTime. The .chat-message:hover .chat-bubble-time CSS fades it in below the bubble, anchored to .chat-message because .chat-bubble's own overflow would clip it."},{"markdown":"A few non-local commands have dedicated desktop handling and must NOT be diverted to the gateway slash pipeline, or they'd lose their behaviour.","startLine":59,"endLine":59,"text":"A few non-local commands have dedicated desktop handling and must NOT be diverted to the gateway slash pipeline, or they'd lose their behaviour."},{"markdown":"The legacy approval responses `/approve` and `/deny` (the `RENDERER_NATIVE_SLASH` set) are excluded from the pipeline and sent as prompt-level input. They remain a compatibility path for text-only backends; structured gateway approvals use the flow below.","startLine":61,"endLine":61,"text":"The legacy approval responses /approve and /deny (the RENDERER_NATIVE_SLASH set) are excluded from the pipeline and sent as prompt-level input. They remain a compatibility path for text-only backends; structured gateway approvals use the flow below."},{"markdown":"Dangerous commands pause the current turn until the user explicitly allows or denies them; the desktop never auto-approves or replays a prompt after an approval request.","startLine":65,"endLine":65,"text":"Dangerous commands pause the current turn until the user explicitly allows or denies them; the desktop never auto-approves or replays a prompt after an approval request."},{"markdown":"[[src/shared/chat-approval.ts#normalizeApprovalRequest]] limits choices to the gateway's offered permissions and preserves a deny path. Dashboard chat renders [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/ApprovalCard.tsx#ApprovalCard]] from `approval.request`. Responses include the gateway-issued `request_id` and runtime session ID through [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useDashboardChatTransport.ts#useDashboardChatTransport]]. Cards queue in arrival order, with an in-flight guard. Only an acknowledgment resolving exactly one request succeeds. Network failures can retry the same ID; a missing ID or unresolved acknowledgment invalidates the cards and interrupts the turn.","startLine":67,"endLine":67,"text":"src/shared/chat-approval.ts#normalizeApprovalRequest limits choices to the gateway's offered permissions and preserves a deny path. Dashboard chat renders src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/ApprovalCard.tsx#ApprovalCard from approval.request. Responses include the gateway-issued request_id and runtime session ID through src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useDashboardChatTransport.ts#useDashboardChatTransport. Cards queue in arrival order, with an in-flight guard. Only an acknowledgment resolving exactly one request succeeds. Network failures can retry the same ID; a missing ID or unresolved acknowledgment invalidates the cards and interrupts the turn."},{"markdown":"Gateway-only WebSocket chat registers opaque renderer IDs through [[src/main/hermes.ts#registerPendingApproval]], bound to the originating renderer and run by [[src/main/ipc/register.ts#registerIpcHandlers]]. These IDs map to the upstream request IDs; they never substitute for them. Completion, cancellation, renderer destruction, or connection loss clears pending requests. Run cleanup retains the originating connection key; cancelled IPC calls settle, and runs that finish before their handle arrives are not registered as active. A transport failure after any approval request cannot replay the prompt. Callers without an approval UI fail closed. `Always allow` requires a second confirmation because the gateway persists that permission.","startLine":69,"endLine":69,"text":"Gateway-only WebSocket chat registers opaque renderer IDs through src/main/hermes.ts#registerPendingApproval, bound to the originating renderer and run by src/main/ipc/register.ts#registerIpcHandlers. These IDs map to the upstream request IDs; they never substitute for them. Completion, cancellation, renderer destruction, or connection loss clears pending requests. Run cleanup retains the originating connection key; cancelled IPC calls settle, and runs that finish before their handle arrives are not registered as active. A transport failure after any approval request cannot replay the prompt. Callers without an approval UI fail closed. Always allow requires a second confirmation because the gateway persists that permission."},{"markdown":"The current upstream `/v1/runs/{run_id}/approval` handler ignores request IDs and resolves the queue head. Desktop therefore stops Runs API turns that request approval, using the original connection's credentials, and directs users to Dashboard chat. Ordinary Runs streaming remains available; manual Runs approvals require an upstream contract change first.","startLine":71,"endLine":71,"text":"The current upstream /v1/runs/{run_id}/approval handler ignores request IDs and resolves the queue head. Desktop therefore stops Runs API turns that request approval, using the original connection's credentials, and directs users to Dashboard chat. Ordinary Runs streaming remains available; manual Runs approvals require an upstream contract change first."},{"markdown":"Dashboard regression tests simulate expired requests and lost acknowledgments with a queued second command, ensuring retries cannot approve that next command and unresolved responses stop the turn.","startLine":75,"endLine":75,"text":"Dashboard regression tests simulate expired requests and lost acknowledgments with a queued second command, ensuring retries cannot approve that next command and unresolved responses stop the turn."},{"markdown":"WebSocket transport tests verify opaque renderer IDs map to gateway IDs, and missing IDs, disconnects, or lost prompt acknowledgments stop the turn without replaying it.","startLine":79,"endLine":79,"text":"WebSocket transport tests verify opaque renderer IDs map to gateway IDs, and missing IDs, disconnects, or lost prompt acknowledgments stop the turn without replaying it."},{"markdown":"Runs transport tests verify approval events stop the original run with its captured credentials, never POST an approval, and never replay through chat completions.","startLine":83,"endLine":83,"text":"Runs transport tests verify approval events stop the original run with its captured credentials, never POST an approval, and never replay through chat completions."},{"markdown":"`/btw` (with aliases `/bg` and `/background`) is a side question that runs on a **concurrent background agent**, so it must never block or queue behind the main turn — that is the point of \"ask without affecting context\".","startLine":87,"endLine":87,"text":"/btw (with aliases /bg and /background) is a side question that runs on a concurrent background agent, so it must never block or queue behind the main turn — that is the point of \"ask without affecting context\"."},{"markdown":"It maps to the gateway's `prompt.background` RPC, which spawns a separate agent and reports back later via a `background.complete` event (a normal `prompt.submit` mid-turn is rejected with \"session busy\"). [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useChatActions.ts#parseBackgroundCommand|parseBackgroundCommand]] detects these commands; `handleSubmitOrQueue` in [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/Chat.tsx]] fires them immediately — bypassing the busy queue — via the shared background flow (also used by the 💭 quick-ask button). The transport's `runBackground` ([[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useDashboardChatTransport.ts#useDashboardChatTransport]]) calls the RPC, and its gateway-event handler renders the `background.complete` answer as a standalone `[bg …]` message. The legacy (non-dashboard) transport has no background RPC and falls back to the blocking quick-ask.","startLine":89,"endLine":89,"text":"It maps to the gateway's prompt.background RPC, which spawns a separate agent and reports back later via a background.complete event (a normal prompt.submit mid-turn is rejected with \"session busy\"). parseBackgroundCommand detects these commands; handleSubmitOrQueue in src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/Chat.tsx fires them immediately — bypassing the busy queue — via the shared background flow (also used by the 💭 quick-ask button). The transport's runBackground (src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useDashboardChatTransport.ts#useDashboardChatTransport) calls the RPC, and its gateway-event handler renders the background.complete answer as a standalone [bg …] message. The legacy (non-dashboard) transport has no background RPC and falls back to the blocking quick-ask."},{"markdown":"The central slash command architecture in [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/handleSlashCommand.ts#handleSlashCommand]] classifies every slash command into a discriminated union (`target: \"desktop\" | \"agent\" | \"model\"`). Unrecognized commands return an error instead of reaching the model as prose.","startLine":93,"endLine":93,"text":"The central slash command architecture in src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/handleSlashCommand.ts#handleSlashCommand classifies every slash command into a discriminated union (target: \"desktop\" | \"agent\" | \"model\"). Unrecognized commands return an error instead of reaching the model as prose."},{"markdown":"The router's attachment guard rejects a command run with staged attachments unless it declares `supportsAttachments`, but `target: \"desktop\"` commands are exempt — they are local UI actions / info displays that never consume attachments (the files stay in the composer for the next message), matching the pre-router behavior where local commands ran unconditionally. Only `agent`/`model` commands, which route content upstream, are gated.","startLine":95,"endLine":95,"text":"The router's attachment guard rejects a command run with staged attachments unless it declares supportsAttachments, but target: \"desktop\" commands are exempt — they are local UI actions / info displays that never consume attachments (the files stay in the composer for the next message), matching the pre-router behavior where local commands ran unconditionally. Only agent/model commands, which route content upstream, are gated."},{"markdown":"The command palette and executor share a catalog built by [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/commandCatalog.ts#createSlashCatalog]]. Hermes Agent metadata comes from `commands.catalog`; Desktop commands are merged after collision validation, and upstream names/aliases are normalized from `/name` to the router's canonical `name`.","startLine":97,"endLine":97,"text":"The command palette and executor share a catalog built by src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/commandCatalog.ts#createSlashCatalog. Hermes Agent metadata comes from commands.catalog; Desktop commands are merged after collision validation, and upstream names/aliases are normalized from /name to the router's canonical name."},{"markdown":"Desktop commands in [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/desktopCommands.ts#DESKTOP_SLASH_COMMANDS]] handle local Electron/renderer UI operations such as opening settings, triggering the active chat's model picker, and switching navigation views without sending prompts.","startLine":101,"endLine":101,"text":"Desktop commands in src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/desktopCommands.ts#DESKTOP_SLASH_COMMANDS handle local Electron/renderer UI operations such as opening settings, triggering the active chat's model picker, and switching navigation views without sending prompts."},{"markdown":"Pure UI desktop actions are flagged `uiAction: true` (settings, model picker, navigation, `/new`, `/clear`, `/fast`). [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useChatActions.ts#useChatActions]] reads that flag to suppress the echoed `/command` user bubble for them — their effect is the UI change itself, so a bubble would be a dangling artifact. Output-producing desktop commands (`/help`, `/memory`, `/usage`, …) are not flagged and still echo, so their output reads as a reply.","startLine":103,"endLine":103,"text":"Pure UI desktop actions are flagged uiAction: true (settings, model picker, navigation, /new, /clear, /fast). src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useChatActions.ts#useChatActions reads that flag to suppress the echoed /command user bubble for them — their effect is the UI change itself, so a bubble would be a dangling artifact. Output-producing desktop commands (/help, /memory, /usage, …) are not flagged and still echo, so their output reads as a reply."},{"markdown":"`/settings <section>` forwards the section name through `openSettings` to [[src/renderer/src/screens/Layout/Layout.tsx]], which opens the global settings modal on the matching nav item (see [[sidebar-navigation#Settings modal]]). [[src/renderer/src/components/settings/SettingsModal.tsx#resolveSection]] maps the argument to a nav id (`appearance`, `privacy`, `connection`, …, plus the legacy alias `hermesagent` → About); an unknown or omitted name lands on the first item.","startLine":105,"endLine":105,"text":"/settings <section> forwards the section name through openSettings to src/renderer/src/screens/Layout/Layout.tsx, which opens the global settings modal on the matching nav item (see sidebar-navigation#Settings modal). src/renderer/src/components/settings/SettingsModal.tsx#resolveSection maps the argument to a nav id (appearance, privacy, connection, …, plus the legacy alias hermesagent → About); an unknown or omitted name lands on the first item."},{"markdown":"Asynchronous Agent commands render a temporary slash-loader bubble without transcript actions such as Copy; the bubble is replaced by the command output or error when execution finishes.","startLine":107,"endLine":107,"text":"Asynchronous Agent commands render a temporary slash-loader bubble without transcript actions such as Copy; the bubble is replaced by the command output or error when execution finishes."},{"markdown":"Agent commands forward upstream via [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/executeAgentCommand.ts#executeAgentCommand]] using gateway JSON-RPC.","startLine":111,"endLine":111,"text":"Agent commands forward upstream via src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/executeAgentCommand.ts#executeAgentCommand using gateway JSON-RPC."},{"markdown":"Model commands and Agent `send`/skill directives pass through [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/prepareModelSubmission.ts#prepareModelSubmission]] before entering the standard chat transport. This is the only slash route allowed to submit model content.","startLine":115,"endLine":115,"text":"Model commands and Agent send/skill directives pass through src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/prepareModelSubmission.ts#prepareModelSubmission before entering the standard chat transport. This is the only slash route allowed to submit model content."},{"markdown":"Visual presentation in the autocomplete popup is handled by [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/SlashCommandIcon.tsx#SlashCommandIcon]], mapping command names to Lucide icons with fallback defaults and a custom SVG registry. Every slash command including desktop settings and navigation shortcuts is assigned an icon.","startLine":119,"endLine":119,"text":"Visual presenta